---
import PostLayout from '../../layouts/PostLayout.astro';
import ParallaxBand from '../../components/ParallaxBand.astro';
---

<PostLayout
  pageTitle="Into the Alps: Innsbruck | Expeditions"
  heroTitle="Into the Alps:<br>Innsbruck"
  heroSubtitle="Weekend getaway options in the Austrian Alps"
  seriesLabel="Into the Alps &mdash; Vol. I"
  heroStyle="background-image: url('https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/05.jpg')"
  date="OCTOBER 9TH, 2021"
  location="Innsbruck, Tyrol, Austria"
  footnote="Our weekend getaway to Innsbruck occurred in the Fall of 2021. &copy; Zubin John"
  moreTitle="More Expeditions"
  description="A weekend in Innsbruck: Altstadt, the City Tower, the Nordkette trail, and Castle Ambras. October 2021."
  ogImage="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/05.jpg"
>
  <Fragment slot="nav-left">Into the Alps</Fragment>
  <a slot="nav-right" class="back-btn" href="/expeditions/">&#8592; All Expeditions</a>

  <!-- SECTION: ALTSTADT (title at the very top) -->
  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title">Altstadt Innsbruck</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="text">
      <p class="lede">
        "The bridge over the Inn" &mdash; that is literally how this town gets its name, after the eponymous river Inn.
        The Tyrolean capital has a history going back at least 800 years, yet in modern times it has built quite a
        reputation as a skiing capital and a hub for all things outdoors.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        The first item on every itinerary has to be a stroll around the Altstadt to soak in the general vibe and the
        gorgeous natural mountain scenery that frames the entire city. The old town sits right at the foot of the
        Nordkette range, making every street corner feel like a painting.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2-UP: Altstadt (06, 013) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/06.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 6" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/013.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 13" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>The heart of the Altstadt, with the iconic Golden Roof at its centre.</figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PARALLAX: City Tower (08, text on top, full width) -->
  <ParallaxBand image="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/08.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 8">
    <h2 slot="title" class="section-title">The City Tower</h2>
    <p class="quote quote-sm">
      For the best views of the city, we made our way up the spiral staircase to the top of the Innsbruck
      Stadtturm. The intricate design, added to the original 450-year-old structure, allows two-way traffic
      and ascends 51 metres to offer panoramic views of the entire city and its surrounding landscape.
    </p>
  </ParallaxBand>

  <!-- 2-UP: City Tower (09 portrait, 07 landscape, wider) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1.5fr;">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/09.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 9" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/07.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 7" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>Views of the river Inn and the Golden Terrace from the top of the Innsbruck Tower.</figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION: NORDKETTE -->
  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title">On the Nordkette Trail</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        Another magical journey is the trip up Innsbruck's local mountain Hafelekar via the Bergbahn. Once up
        in the Nordkettes, on a clear day you can catch views extending far into the Karwendel Mountains and
        down into the valley below. If you are lucky, you might even encounter a herd of Wild Ibex.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2+1: Nordkette (01, 11 top, 10 full width) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2plus1">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/01.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 1" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/11.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 11" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="span-2">
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/10.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 10" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>The ascent on the Hungerburgbahn and Nordkettenbahn, and the alpine landscape that greets you at the top.</figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION: CASTLE AMBRAS (heading removed, paragraph kept) -->
  <section class="space-sm" style="padding-top:44px;">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        Rounding out the trip was a short excursion outside the city centre to Schloss Ambras, known for housing
        the eccentric collection of Archduke Ferdinand II. The castle is a fine example of German Renaissance
        architecture and is most famous for its Spanish Hall and an extensive Habsburg Portrait gallery.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2-UP: Castle Ambras (02, 03) -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/02.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 2" /></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/03.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 3" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>The grounds of Schloss Ambras, with the Inn valley stretching out below.</figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION: AUF WIEDERSEHEN -->
  <section class="space-sm" style="padding-top:44px;">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title">Auf Wiedersehen</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SINGLE: centred image (04), no caption -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="single">
      <figure>
        <div class="media"><img src="https://media.bifunctional.xyz/expeditions/innsbruck/04.jpg" alt="Into the Alps: Innsbruck photo 4" /></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MORE CARDS -->
  <Fragment slot="more-cards">
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/salzburg/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Into the Alps: Salzburg</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Published &mdash; Oct 2021</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Untersberg, Hohensalzburg, and the Sound of Music</p>
    </a>
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/verona/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Verona</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Published &mdash; Oct 2020</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Of Bridges and Brawls</p>
    </a>
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/bangkok/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Bangkok Airwaves</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Published &mdash; Mar 2019</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Wat Pho, Wat Arun, Phra Nakhon district</p>
    </a>
  </Fragment>
</PostLayout>
